{
  "_comment": "Master-data seed manifest. Tables are extracted from the source instance and loaded onto the target in this order. Scope = records created inside any 'windows' range (2026-08-22 is skipped: plugin activation day, run as admin), ANDed with the table's 'query'. 'key' is the business key used to detect a record that already exists on the target with a different sys_id; on_conflict 'fail' stops the load, 'adopt' keeps the target's record (used for join rows that platform automation may already have created). 'insert_as' gives temporary values used on insert; the real values are applied after every table is loaded (e.g. children can only be added while a price list is draft). Specs with 'source_instance' + 'scope_query' (940-971, transactional quotes/orders) are read from that instance by explicit record numbers instead of the created-on windows; platform-generated children (related parties, addresses, allocations, snapshots, approvals, order tasks) are not seeded because the platform recreates them.",
